   "mechanism": "Mucosal infections in the gut involve antigen sensing by ITGAX (CD11c) positive dendritic cells. This process initiates CARD9-dependent innate immune signaling. CARD9 activation upregulates the expression and secretion of TNFSF13 (APRIL), a cytokine that drives B-cell class switching to IgA. The resulting overproduction of poorly O-galactosylated IgA1 is the primary systemic driver of IgA glomerulonephritis.",
