   "mechanism": "The deposition of IgA immune complexes in the kidney triggers the alternative complement pathway. CFH normally regulates this cascade, but genetic variants impair its inhibitory function, leading to unchecked generation of complement cleavage fragments like iC3b. iC3b binds to its receptor CR4 (which contains ITGAX) on infiltrating macrophages in the glomerulus, driving local inflammation and exacerbating IgA glomerulonephritis.",
